{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics","id":919890,"title":"What skill for mathematics and statistics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-23T13:09:38-07:00","id":919890,"title":"What skill for mathematics and statistics?","content":"I had hoped this would get handled with the new CofD book, but, alas, I cannot find anything. So, I am reaching out to you all, in hopes that someone was able to find something in the text. If not in the text, the perhaps someone knows of an OPP/WW employee/writer/etc that might have spoken on the matter?<br /> <br /> In the CofD core book, there is a reference to economics in Academics, but that's the closest it gets to math. Science, meanwhile, includes several fields of science (biology, physics, etc) which doubtlessly use statistical models to explain data. My gut says that this would be up to the storyteller, and up to the player to define what &quot;sort&quot; of math they are using. But, do you all know anything different?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12020-skewskewskew","name":"skewskewskew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:14:27-07:00","id":919895,"title":"","content":"I'd lean towards Science over Academics overall, if for no other reason than my games typically see more opportunities to apply other fields of Academics than they do other fields of Science. Your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> What raw mathematical actions have come up in your game, out of curiosity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:21:42-07:00","id":919900,"title":"","content":"Don't bother finding a skill for all mathematics, just use the mental skill that makes most sense in context. Calculating important engineering stuff? Crafts+Intelligence. Economy and probability? Academics. Chemistry related math? Science. Rocket science and quantum physics? Science. And so on.<br /> And, most importantly, allow a &quot;sister skill&quot; to apply. Dude with Science might calculate that Crafts stuff too, why not? If you feel it's robbing one of the skills, just apply a penalty to the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:23:11-07:00","id":919901,"title":"","content":"My games tend to use a lot of Science. Mostly to determine what's happening when you're looking at a particular phenomena, or coming up with the lexicon used to describe something that's happening.<br /> <br /> I second math-as-Science rather than Academics. A good rule of thumb is that Academics are the &quot;psychological&quot; sciences, such as study of group behaviors, history, art theory, color theory, and so on - Academics will tell you that green's complementary color is purple and that many New Age cultures see it as the color of life, as well as its etymology and that some cultures have the same word for blue and green. Science will tell you that green is between 490 and 700-something nanometers light wavelength (one of the broader frequencies), and that it's the most efficient available type of natural chlorophyll for plants in regards to our sun for absorption of light, and that most public laser outputs are in this spectrum because they are neodymium-doped yttrium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:23:44-07:00","id":919902,"title":"","content":"I'm not an OPP employee or freelancer, but I'm a fan who likes to think she has a pretty good handle on the rules. There's really no &quot;Mathematics Skill&quot;, but as you observed, math is involved in a couple of other mental Skills. Academics, Science, and Computers, all involve math to some degree, and it can even be useful in Crafts and Investigation. I would say depending on what the player is trying to accomplish, pick the Skill that seems like the best fit for the situation. If you've got a player who has a character concept to which exceptional mathematical aptitude is an important detail, consider taking Mathematics as an Academics or Science Specialty, along with the Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Specialty Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:32:31-07:00","id":919912,"title":"","content":"Remember that by forcing all Math related things into Science, you are kinda encouraging the model where characters are required to have 1 dot of Science / Academics to perform basic academic tasks. While it's one way to do things, I feel that CofD moved away from 1 being &quot;bare minimum&quot; to &quot;wow, you've got a 1 in this skill, that's pretty nice, you can do a lot with it!&quot;. Like, you couldn't portray field I'm studying without literally handling every of our students 1 dot in Academics (for the &quot;soft&quot; side of it), Science (we deal with math, probability, simulations and other stuff too, yo), Investigation and Politics. And a dot of Medicine and Brawl too, I guess.<br /> <br /> Which in CofD has a side problem of making people like this into Sherlock Holmes level of dillettantes, because mechanically, there is no difference between taking Science for Quantum Physics and for taking it for doing math. I feel that it's easier to portray a &quot;field&quot; by using one of the big mental skills, and applying more and more penalties as it goes away from it's &quot;core&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:35:51-07:00","id":919915,"title":"","content":"Math should even be allowed with a few of the non-Mental Skills. Expression for example, covers a number of fields that require at least some basic math knowledge, and can involve a lot of math depending on your approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:44:10-07:00","id":919922,"title":"","content":"Yeah, CofD really shines if you look at dots on the sheet having the &quot;CHARACTER CONCEPT&quot; field in mind and allow yourself as a GM some flexibility. Instead of asking &quot;do you have skill XYZ for it?&quot;, I started having much more fun as GM and player alike by switching to &quot;which part of your character allows you to do that?&quot;<br /> With &quot;which part&quot; being both represented by character background and fluff, and their dots. They exist to...a hard word that means things are supposed to make each other better and work in tandem :&lt;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:55:35-07:00","id":919930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=919902#post919902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not an OPP employee or freelancer, but I'm a fan who likes to think she has a pretty good handle on the rules. There's really no &quot;Mathematics Skill&quot;, but as you observed, math is involved in a couple of other mental Skills. Academics, Science, and Computers, all involve math to some degree, and it can even be useful in Crafts and Investigation. I would say depending on what the player is trying to accomplish, pick the Skill that seems like the best fit for the situation. If you've got a player who has a character concept to which exceptional mathematical aptitude is an important detail, consider taking Mathematics as an Academics or Science Specialty, along with the Area of Expertise and Interdisciplinary Specialty Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Skill specialties are exactly what I was considering. My character is a math whizz, and has possibly studied many other topics, but math has been a passion, focus, etc. Where do I even apply that spec, in order to take Area of Expertise? I think &quot;either or&quot; is a good enough answer for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12020-skewskewskew","name":"skewskewskew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T14:00:33-07:00","id":919935,"title":"","content":"I'd say that it probably falls into Academics more than Science.<br /> <br /> Yes, raw calculation would be an Intelligence + Science roll... but I can count <i>on my fingers</i> how many times I had to do difficult calculations for my higher level courses.<br /> <br /> Take, for example:<br /> <br /> (1) Solve c\u00b2u<sub>xx</sub> + u<sub>tt</sub> = 0 for the initial functions u(x,0) = p(x) and u<sub>x</sub>(x,0) = q(x).<br /> (2) Let <i>E/F</i> be a Galois extension, and <i>L</i> an intermediate subfield, such that <i>L/F</i> is a normal extension. Prove that the restriction map <i>\u03c1:Aut<sub>F</sub>(E) \u2192 Aut<sub>F</sub>(L)</i> given by <i>\u03c1(\u03c4) = \u03c4|<sub>L</sub></i>, is a surjective homomorphism.<br /> <br /> (1) would be a Science roll to solve (and should be easy enough for any engineer in the audience), while (2) would be an Academics roll.<br /> <br /> [algebraist_neckbeard]And (2) is <i>real</i> math, not engineer scribbles like (2).[/algebraist_neckbeard]<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Basically, &quot;my character is one who does math&quot; is folded into multiple skills, while &quot;math is what my character does&quot; is Academics. Kind of like how &quot;my character is one who writes&quot; is folded into a crapton of skills, while &quot;writing is what my character does&quot; is Expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T14:14:49-07:00","id":919938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=919935#post919935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>EDIT:</b> Basically, &quot;my character is one who does math&quot; is folded into multiple skills, while &quot;math is what my character does&quot; is Academics. Kind of like how &quot;my character is one who writes&quot; is folded into a crapton of skills, while &quot;writing is what my character does&quot; is Expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I follow this. Are you saying, to be a good writer, you'd need a variety of skills, but to do the actual writing, you use Expression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12020-skewskewskew","name":"skewskewskew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T14:26:54-07:00","id":919941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skewskewskew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=919930#post919930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill specialties are exactly what I was considering. My character is a math whizz, and has possibly studied many other topics, but math has been a passion, focus, etc. Where do I even apply that spec, in order to take Area of Expertise? I think &amp;quot;either or&amp;quot; is a good enough answer for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, either Academics or Science would probably be appropriate. Better yet, with Interdisciplinary Specialty you can apply the bonus to both, and any other skill rolls where it would be appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T15:11:52-07:00","id":919969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skewskewskew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=919938#post919938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I follow this. Are you saying, to be a good writer, you'd need a variety of skills, but to do the actual writing, you use Expression?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly - what I'm saying is that a novelist, say, would have a high rating in Expression - the &quot;art&quot; of writing falls under Expression. Meanwhile, Mr. Biologist over there without any dots in Expression can still write, no problem - it's just that he'd be unable to write a decent poem or a good novel.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you don't <i>need</i> Academics to do the little bit of math and computation that pretty much everything requires - but if you want to be able to intelligently discuss the Taniyama-Shimura Conjecture, or need to know the finer points of chaotic maps, then you better have a decent Academics rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:08:25-07:00","id":920130,"title":"","content":"Am I alone in thinking Investigation is the most appropriate Skill for standard arithmetic/algebra/trigonometry/calculus stuff divorced from the context of a more immediate Skill like Crafts or Science?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:35:16-07:00","id":920144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920130#post920130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I alone in thinking Investigation is the most appropriate Skill for standard arithmetic/algebra/trigonometry/calculus stuff divorced from the context of a more immediate Skill like Crafts or Science?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, Enigmas is!<br /> <br /> But we don't have Enigmas in the present.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can kind of vaguely see where you're coming from, though.<br /> <br /> (I do kinda want to houserule-replace Computers with Enigmas. It actually feels more... complete that way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:04:40-07:00","id":920344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920144#post920144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, Enigmas is!<br /> <br /> But we don't have Enigmas in the present.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can kind of vaguely see where you're coming from, though.<br /> <br /> (I do kinda want to houserule-replace Computers with Enigmas. It actually feels more... complete that way.)</div> </div> </div> </div>But in the age of Google and StackOverflow, is not Computers already Enigmas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:33:57-07:00","id":920364,"title":"","content":"If math should fall under Enigmas, and Enigmas became Computers, should math fall under Computers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I rule most math as falling under Computers, myself; I might be swayed the something like proof-building falls under Academics, or planning/drafting/measuring falls under Crafts or Science. But any sort of calculations/problem-solving/number-crunching goes with Computers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:49:55-07:00","id":920426,"title":"","content":"Precisely! Hence, get rid of Computers, and replace it with Enigmas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920364#post920364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If math should fall under Enigmas, and Enigmas became Computers, should math fall under Computers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If knowledge of Christianity falls under Religion, and Religion became Science, should knowledge of Christianity fall under Science? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And saying &quot;most&quot; math like that wounds me. In my cold, flinty soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T10:08:04-07:00","id":920435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920426#post920426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If knowledge of Christianity falls under Religion, and Religion became Science, should knowledge of Christianity fall under Science? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, swapping Science for Religion in historical settings was always a weird choice. Religious studies were already covered under Academics and Occult (depending on the religion), and it's not like ancient cultures didn't do Science. It may not have been as advanced as modern science, but neither was ancient Medicine, and that Skill stuck around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T10:29:58-07:00","id":920446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920435#post920435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, swapping Science for Religion in historical settings was always a weird choice. Religious studies were already covered under Academics and Occult (depending on the religion), and it's not like ancient cultures didn't do Science. It may not have been as advanced as modern science, but neither was ancient Medicine, and that Skill stuck around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think Dark Eras did right on that part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T11:47:07-07:00","id":920475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920426#post920426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If knowledge of Christianity falls under Religion, and Religion became Science, should knowledge of Christianity fall under Science? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And saying &quot;most&quot; math like that wounds me. In my cold, flinty soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>By (mis)application of the transitive property*, yes, yes it should. Same for why there should be a Horses specialty under Drive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I took one year of math where they made me do proofs, then got scared and ran away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T15:18:59-07:00","id":920583,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of using Investigation. When I was doing &quot;get a degree&quot; thing, I believe the most difficult part of creating a useful statistical model was deciding on all the various elements that should go into it. What do you account for, what do you not, how do you check against biases (and skews omg). That sort of investigation could be investigation! I like it.<br /> <br /> Computers, though, also, yes, because no one's doing regression by hand anymore (dear god) and being tech savvy really did make a big difference there.<br /> <br /> Thank you all!<br /> <br /> (And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>, I do understand your explanation, thanks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12020-skewskewskew","name":"skewskewskew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T15:21:06-07:00","id":920584,"title":"","content":"I've always seen Academics as being the Humanities, personally. Math would definitely be a Science roll at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T16:18:20-07:00","id":920618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>skewskewskew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=920583#post920583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because no one's doing regression by hand anymore (dear god)</div> </div> </div> </div>Challenge accepted!<br /> <br /> (No really - I did most of my statistics coursework with minimal calculator use and a <i>lot</i> of paper. If you handed me an abacus or a slide-rule, I'd probably use those in preference to the calculator.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T14:04:38-07:00","id":921147,"title":"","content":"Thinking more on subject - I can totally see Investigation as math Skill. Investigation is, basically, data analyze Skill and is used to solve sodoku and crosswords - and each math problem is puzzle to solve, in the end. You apply data, use common methods to process it, until you get clues ( 'variable x should be approximately...').<br /> <br /> In contrast, Science and Academics Skills are all about hard facts and 'lore' of their discipline. Chemist knows atomic number of whole periodic table - but to solve proportion on structure problem he still would use rather Investigation to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:22:02-07:00","id":921192,"title":"","content":"I think that's just a further illustration of why it's best to not try to pin down math as something that is governed by a single Skill; even in just a default/primary state.<br /> <br /> Investigation is used for problem solving and puzzles yes, but as you say, Academics and Science are where you get the &quot;hard facts&quot; which in this case means the rules of mathematics. Without Academics/Science, the Investigation user has enough basic knowledge of math for things like simple puzzles, but doesn't inherently know how to use calculus to generate quadratic surfaces, or how to apply n-dimensional hypercubes to biological speciation. The rules and logic behind those requires training in the subject matter.<br /> <br /> Forcing every concept that relies on a Skill that uses a good deal of math to also have to invest in Investigation just to be good at the math part isn't generally fun/great for play. If you want to play Indiana Jones so you have high Academics and Investigation, that's cool. But if you're playing an architect, you shouldn't have to invest in Investigation for when you need to roll to figure out the engineering numbers for your big project.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T06:46:55-07:00","id":921977,"title":"","content":"I'm in the &quot;daily application of mathematics was enigmas, has been supplanted by computers&quot; camp. I think daily application is key here, as mathematicians aren't accountants, or businessmen. If it's pure math (Calculus) I'd be inclined to go with Academics, but if it's a math as applied to Science, such as most theoretical physics is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T06:55:59-07:00","id":921980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/919890-what-skill-for-mathematics-and-statistics?p=921977#post921977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's pure math (Calculus)</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally <i>all my hate</i>. Like, I actually feel a little bit personally insulted here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}